2Co 12:1 , For commending of his apostleship, though he might glory of his wonderful revelations
2Co 12:9 , yet he rather chooses to glory of his infirmities;
2Co 12:11 , blaming them for forcing him to this vain boasting;
2Co 12:14 , He promises to come to them again; but yet altogether in the affection of a father;
2Co 12:20 , although he fears he shall to his grief find many offenders, and public disorders there.
